      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the usual maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Maximum dose:** The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release in many labels). It is usually split into doses of 850 mg or less, and no single dose should be more than 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis could be a typo. Some possible intended doses:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided into two doses\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. I'll enter the order once you do. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
