       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and no metformin protocol I know of supports 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the maximum labeled dose, and a single 1,700 mg dose is well above the usual 1,000 mg ceiling. The risk is serious: lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within labeled limits.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or another dose you choose.\n- **Route the order through pharmacy.** If a protocol really does exist, the pharmacist who reviewed it can enter or co-sign the order. Alternatively, you can cite the protocol document in the order note.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
